                <pb facs="0487" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg391"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ch. Weymann &amp; Co. to the
                            Mayor.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith we beg to hand you the sum of $75,
                    being the amount of additional taxes you claim on our three foreign clerks,
                    which we pay under protest.</p>
                <p>At the same time we beg to inform you that we have laid our claim before the
                    American minister.</p>
                <p>We have the honor to remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ch. Weymann</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
